{
  "title": "Advanced Linux: Security and Hardening",
  "description": "The advanced follow-up to Linux Fundamentals, for administrators and developers who run Linux servers. You will learn to threat-model a server and reduce its attack surface, store and check passwords properly with PAM, write sudo rules that can't be escaped, lock SSH down to keys and ban scanners with fail2ban, find and fix privilege-escalation paths (setuid, capabilities, ACLs), confine programs with AppArmor and SELinux, build a default-deny nftables firewall, sandbox services with systemd, record what matters with auditd, detect tampering, prioritize patches, harden the kernel and run containers safely. The course ends with a read-only audit script and a practical incident-response guide. Every topic comes with a commented, ready-to-adapt configuration file.",
